---
/*
 * Section 6 — who we work with.
 *
 * THE LOCATION PARAGRAPH IS DELETED IN FULL. Approved copy sets a second body block
 * here: "Based in Metro Vancouver. We work remotely across Canada, and on site within
 * the Lower Mainland where the work benefits from it." Fredrick's instruction of Aug 25
 * 2026 takes the location line and everything like it off the visible site, confirmed
 * again on Aug 26 when this page was planned.
 *
 * It went WHOLE rather than half-kept, and that is the same call made on /accounting's
 * FAQ: the paragraph was about where we are, so trimming it to "we work remotely across
 * Canada, and on site where the work benefits from it" would leave a sentence whose
 * subject had been removed — on site relative to what? A question with nothing behind it
 * is worse than no question. One consequence worth knowing: the on-site-in-the-Lower-
 * Mainland offer existed only in that paragraph and is now published nowhere.
 *
 * Two other places on this page lost the same thing — the hero subhead and section 3's
 * fourth chip. They travel together with the four other removals on the homepage and
 * /accounting. Do not restore one alone.
 *
 * THE LINK TO /accounting is the one the copy file's SEO section asks for, carried on
 * "there's a page for that" — which is the sentence that already points at it, so the
 * link goes where the reader is looking rather than being appended.
 *
 * "THE WORK GENERALIZES FURTHER THAN ONE SECTOR, BECAUSE THE PATTERN DOES" is the line
 * that stops this page reading as an accounting firm's supplier. Keep it last.
 */
---

<section class="section section--stage who" id="who-we-work-with">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head who__head">
      <h2 class="section__title who__title">
        Small and mid-sized businesses, and professional practices.
      </h2>
      <p class="section__lede who__lede">
        Businesses large enough that administrative work has become a real cost, and small
        enough that nobody has a department to hand it to. Accounting and bookkeeping
        practices are the sector we&rsquo;ve built for most deliberately, and
        <a href="/accounting">there&rsquo;s a page for that</a>. The work generalizes
        further than one sector, because the pattern does.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .who__head {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .who__title {
    max-width: 26ch;
  }

  .who__lede a {
    color: var(--ark-terracotta-ink);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Two columns: heading left, the paragraph right, running to the same right edge. With
   * the location paragraph removed this section is a heading and one paragraph, which
   * stacked would leave most of the band empty. */
  @media (min-width: 901px) and (orientation: landscape) {
    .who__head {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
      column-gap: 56px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .who__title {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 1;
    }

    .who__lede {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1;
      /* Beside the heading, not under it. */
      margin-top: 2px;
      max-width: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .who__lede {
      max-width: 44ch;
    }
  }
</style>
